  "title": "Accenture Plc (ACN): 3Q Preview: Macro headwinds likely to pressure FY26 guidance",
  "type": "earnings_preview",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-06-03",
  "insights": [
   "Goldman Sachs expects Accenture to narrow its FY26 constant currency revenue growth guidance to 3.0%-4.0% (from 3.0%-5.0%) due to prolonged macro headwinds and slower client decision-making observed in April/May.",
   "Investors are viewed as negatively positioned on ACN and the broader IT Services group ahead of the June 18 earnings print.",
   "While Outsourcing backlog remains solid, a potential slowdown in Consulting bookings is identified as a key swing factor for FY27 guidance.",
   "GS lowered EPS estimates for FY26/27/28 to $13.70/$14.55/$15.95 (from $13.90/$15.05/$16.50) and reduced the 12-month price target to $270 from $300."
