  "source": "Goldman Sachs",
  "title": "Apple Inc. (AAPL): WWDC 2026 preview: Expect focus on AI feature progress & enhanced Siri details",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "high",
  "published": "2026-06-03",
  "insights": [
   "Apple is expected to announce a new AI-enhanced Siri at WWDC26, featuring on-screen awareness, personal context, and a new chat-based interface.",
   "The new AI features are viewed as key medium-term demand drivers for the iPhone and potential catalysts for new Services revenue streams.",
   "Apple is expected to confirm a launch timeline for AI Siri alongside the premium iPhone 18 family in September 2026.",
   "The company is likely to announce user-selectable model providers for Apple Intelligence features, reinforcing Apple's role as a critical consumer distribution channel for AI models.",
   "Additional AI features expected include sophisticated photo editing tools (Extend, enhance, Reframe), improved Visual Intelligence in the Camera app, and new Safari/Wallet functionality.",
   "Apple's 'Private Cloud Compute' and a focus on token efficiency are expected to highlight the company's strategy for on-device processing to ensure privacy and manage costs."
  ],
  "market_movers": [
   {
    "ticker": "AAPL",
    "action": "reiterate",
    "rating": "Buy",
    "price_target": "$340",
    "rationale": "The market's focus on slower product revenue growth masks the strength of the Apple ecosystem, revenue durability, and the inflection point in the Services investment narrative.",
    "conviction": "medium"
   }
  ],
  "earnings": [
   "iPhone revenue grew +23% yoy in F1H26.",
   "Services are expected to drive the majority of gross profit growth over the next 5 years."
