 {
  "source": "Goldman Sachs",
  "title": "AstraZeneca (AZN.L): ASCO takes: Incremental update on SERENA-6; readacross from persevERA to SERENA-4 mixed",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-06-03",
  "insights": [
   "Updated SERENA-6 data presented at ASCO showed 99% reduction in total ctDNA by Week 8 in the treatment group vs. 64% increase in control, but failed to address FDA/ODAC concerns regarding trial design and modest OS benefit.",
   "The firm views the SERENA-6 update as incremental and maintains caution regarding the FDA approval decision due to the lack of a PDUFA date and underpowered final OS analysis.",
   "The persevERA trial (Roche) readacross to SERENA-4 is viewed as neutral/slightly negative due to a disappointing PFS HR of 0.89, suggesting SERDs may have limited effect in this setting.",
   "Despite the negative readacross, SERENA-4 may still show statistically significant PFS benefits due to a larger trial size and a potentially weaker control arm compared to persevERA."
  ],
  "market_movers": [
   {
    "ticker": "AZN",
    "action": "reiterate",
    "rating": "Buy",
    "price_target": "16,525p / $219",
    "rationale": "The firm maintains a Buy rating despite incremental data updates, modeling $5.5bn in peak unrisked adjusted sales for camizestrant.",
